.venv/
__pycache__/
# Written by the MCP framework itself at runtime (the FTS index). Copying a host-built one in
# would ship an index whose cache key does not match this image's HEAD, so it would be
# discarded and rebuilt on first request anyway.
_meta/.cache/
# Generated at deploy time by the pages workflow; never needed at runtime.
site/
# 6 MB of Parquet that the SERVER never opens. It is the build-and-analysis artifact:
# ingest_expenditures.py writes it and build_documents.py reads it to generate the 544
# agency-year documents, both offline. At serve time actuals are proxied LIVE from Socrata
# (see src/budget_backend.py), so the mirror is not a fallback the server can reach for --
# the Dockerfile already says this and now the build context matches.
data/
# NOTE: .git is deliberately NOT ignored -- it is a RUNTIME dependency. The FTS cache key is
# `git rev-parse HEAD` plus a hash of `git status --porcelain`, and corpus_overview() shells
# out to `git log -1`. Without it, repo_state() collapses to a constant, which means content
# changes are never picked up for the life of the process and corpus_overview reports an empty
# commit -- silently, in both cases. Build from a depth-1 clone to keep it small.
